# DTF tier manifest: admin-collision-2875
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. No SSO stack needed -- the oracle seeds the
# federated principal directly in the DB (docker exec psql) and drives the real
# startup code path by restarting the backend container.
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS (#2875): startup `provision_admin_user` (backend/src/main.rs)
# must never mutate a FEDERATED (SSO) identity when maintaining the built-in
# local admin. The built-in admin is keyed on username='admin'; before the fix,
# a federated user holding that username (natural under SKIP_ADMIN_PROVISIONING,
# or when the IdP preferred_username is 'admin') was hijacked on the next
# restart: its auth_provider was flipped to 'local' and the built-in admin
# password stamped onto it, merging the two identities into one admin account
# (cross-identity privilege escalation / account takeover).
#
# Discriminating oracle (DB truth, not HTTP codes):
#   The only 'admin' row is a FEDERATED user (auth_provider='oidc', external_id
#   set, is_admin=true, no password). Restart the backend to run
#   provision_admin_user, then assert that row is UNCHANGED.
#     * GREEN on the fixed image: existence check ignores federated admins and
#       the guarded upsert refuses to clobber -> row stays oidc, external_id
#       intact, password still NULL.
#     * RED on a pre-#2875 image: the row is flipped to auth_provider='local'
#       and a password_hash is stamped on -> the identities are merged.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
